-- A `never` signed with the wrong hazard, `tolerates loss`. `velle validate` refuses it:
--
--   - The compiler cannot read it: a never signs 'tolerates contention' only (OQ40), found LIDENT('loss') (at 12:44)
--
-- The message ends its rule with "(OQ40)", a settled question in `working-docs/QUESTIONS.md`
-- that means nothing to the author, and names the token as "LIDENT", a word of the parser.
-- The text is written in `compiler/src/main/kotlin/velle/Parser.kt`, `parseToleratesContention`.
act Member {
    name: text
    balance: decimal
}
never (Member where balance < 0) tolerates loss
